::Q1::Which is a practical EC2 security measure? 
{
=Restricting network access to necessary ports and sources
~Disabling authentication
~Sharing administrator credentials
~Opening every port to the internet
}

::Q2::What does encryption at rest protect? 
{
~Only IAM usernames
=Data while it is stored
~Only data being transmitted over a network
~Only EC2 instance types
}

::Q3::What does encryption in transit protect? 
{
=Data while it moves between systems
~Only database table definitions
~Only data stored on disk
~Only S3 object names
}

::Q4::What does multi factor authentication add to account security? 
{
~A second S3 bucket
~A second EC2 instance
~A second database
=An additional authentication factor beyond a password
}

::Q5::Why should security groups be restricted? 
{
~To remove all network controls
~To make every address trusted
=To limit network access to the ports and sources that are actually needed
~To increase the number of exposed services
}